At 08:51 PM 12/20/02 -0500, Pierre Abbat wrote:
>I am currently revising and attempting to prove the validity of the valfendi
>algorithm.

A new person not going to know that "valfendi algorithm" means (to you, 
since I've never seen it before) an algorithm to break a speech stream into 
individual words.

>/varKIClafLO'i/ is lexed as either an error

It is an error because no word can have two valid stresses.  If there is 
secondary stress, it cannot be confuseable with primary stress.

>{varkicla *flo'i} or the correct {varkiclaflo'i} "hovercraft"

lujvo interpretations always take precedent over an interpretation 
including a fu'ivla.

